/-!
# Higher direct images of the twists on a projective bundle, outside the relative dimension

Let `S` be a scheme, let `n` be a natural number, let `E` be an `𝒪_S`-module which is finite
locally free of constant rank `n + 1`, and let `π : 𝐏(E) = Proj_S(Sym(E)) ⟶ S` be the structure
morphism of its projective bundle. For every integer `d` the higher direct images
`R^q π_* 𝒪_{𝐏(E)}(d)` of a twist of the structure sheaf vanish in every degree `q` outside the
range `0 ≤ q ≤ n`: below zero because a right derived functor vanishes in negative degrees, and
above `n` because `π⁻¹(V)` is covered by `n + 1` affine opens with affine finite intersections
whenever `E` is trivial over `V`, so the Čech degree bound of [Stacks, Tag 071L] applies.

The intermediate results are stated for an arbitrary quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `A`
whose ring of homogeneous sections over the opens of a basis of `S` is generated by `k` elements
of degree one; the projective bundle of a finite locally free module of rank `n + 1` is the case
`k = n + 1`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleVanishing.inf_basicOpen_eq_basicOpen_prod`: a finite
  nonempty intersection of standard opens of a projective spectrum is the standard open of the
  product of the elements.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleVanishing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_piece`:
  the higher direct images of a homogeneous twist on a relative projective spectrum vanish in
  degrees at least `k`, given `k` degree-one generators over a basis of the base.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleVanishing.exists_span_sections`: a module whose
  restriction to an open is finite free has, over that open, a spanning family of sections
  indexed by the basis of the free module.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleVanishing.exists_span_sectionPieces_one`: over an
  affine open trivializing `E`, the degree-one homogeneous sections of `Sym(E)` are spanned by
  `n + 1` elements.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleVanishing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_twist`:
  **`R^q π_* 𝒪_{𝐏(E)}(d) = 0` for `q < 0` and for `q > n`**, for every scheme `S`, every `E`
  finite locally free of constant rank `n + 1` and every integer `d`.

## Implementation notes

The twist data is a parameter. `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.TwistData` is the
structure of [Stacks, Tag 01NR]; the statements below are the general form of the assertion, of
which the statement for any particular glued family of twists is an instance. This is the
convention of every other result about these twists, for instance
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjFlat.isFlatOver_twist`, and of the invertibility of the
twists on a projective bundle,
`Stacks.SymGraded.twistData_isInvertible_schemeSheafGradedAlgebra`.

**Every `D : TwistData` binder below is satisfiable**, so the statements are not vacuous: the
existence assertion of Tag 01NR is proved, unconditionally:
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GluedTwistAlgebra.twistDataOfGradedAlgebra`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/GluedTwistAlgebra/Assemble.lean:521`) produces a `TwistData A`
for an arbitrary `A : SheafGradedAlgebra S` "on no hypothesis beyond the graded algebra itself",
the nested cocycle of Tag 01MZ being discharged by `ProjTwistCocycle.isNestedCocycle`. So every
`D` binder here is instantiable from this repository — in particular at
`A = Stacks.SymGraded.schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc` — and `isQuasicoherentPieces_free`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SheafSymmetricAlgebra/Free.lean:180`) discharges `hqc` for a free
module, so the registration below is non-vacuous at `ℰ = 𝒪_S^{n+1}`.

A `TwistData` also carries, as its `chartData` field, the identification
`Scheme.Modules.restrict (D.algebra.piece d) ((relativeProj A).chart U hU) ≅`
`twistingSheaf (A.grading U) d`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.ChartData.chartIso`,
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjTwists/Statement.lean:179`). That is the input a
computation of `R^q π_*` in the middle range `1 ≤ q ≤ n - 1` needs and the Čech degree bound
used below does not; that computation is
`ProjectiveBundleCohomology.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_twist_of_ne`
in `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjectiveBundleCohomology/LocalModel.lean`).

The covering of `π⁻¹(V)` is taken to be the images under the affine chart of the standard opens
of the absolute projective spectrum of the section ring, exactly as in the flatness argument
quoted above. What the degree bound needs beyond that is an affine covering of every finite
intersection of the members, and here a single open suffices: the intersection of the standard
opens at `x i`, `i ∈ s`, is the standard open at `∏_{i ∈ s} x i`, a homogeneous element of
degree `#s > 0`, so it is affine on the nose and the bound `#s + 1 - 1 ≤ k` is just `#s ≤ k`.

Several proofs below install a local `Module` instance with `inferInstanceAs`. The sections of a
sheaf of modules over an open carry one module structure through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.instModule` and another through the `ModuleCat` that the
underlying presheaf of modules records; the two are the same term, but the spellings of the ring
of scalars differ and instance search, which unfolds only reducible definitions, does not bridge
them. This is the same device as `Stacks.SymGraded.module_sections_siteRing`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 071L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/071L)
-/

